<h1 class="fs-37 lh-37 mb-24">Layouts</h1>
<p class="mb-32">Arrange the main regions of a page, then compose cards and other components inside them. Each example includes a live preview and matching HTML.</p>
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Posts with a right sidebar</h2>
<p class="mb-24">An archive section holds two post summaries, followed by a related-reading sidebar. <code>grid</code> enables the layout, and <code>grid-sidebar-right-lg-344px</code> sets <code>minmax(0, 1fr) 344px</code> from 960 pixels. Below that, the sidebar stacks after the posts. <code>gap-40</code> supplies the 40-pixel gap at the default root font size.</p>
{% set sidebar %}{% include "components/layouts/right-sidebar.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(sidebar, "Main content with right sidebar") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Three column</h2>
<p class="mb-24">A section heading followed by three existing vertical cards. <code>flex-md</code> switches the parent to flex from 820 pixels, and <code>flex-1</code> on each wrapper shares the available row width equally. Below medium the cards stack. <code>gap-24</code> separates columns, and <code>mb-24</code> separates stacked cards.</p>
{% set three %}{% include "components/layouts/three-column.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(three, "Three column") }}
<p class="mb-24">The cards share the spacing lesson and retain their 344-pixel maximum width.</p>
<p>Layout section headings use <code>h2</code>; the cards retain their <code>h3</code> headings.</p>
</article>
